1
00:00:00,500 --> 00:00:04,106
Welcome to Module 14, where we
finish setting up your account.

2
00:00:04,106 --> 00:00:08,526
In this lesson, we'll buy a business
phone number, forward its calls to you,

3
00:00:08,526 --> 00:00:13,063
and make sure carriers trust it, so your
calls get answered and your texts get

4
00:00:13,063 --> 00:00:13,644
delivered.

5
00:00:14,501 --> 00:00:16,653
Open Settings, then Phone System.

6
00:00:16,653 --> 00:00:21,609
A Kyntlo number means every call and
text is saved on the customer's record,

7
00:00:21,609 --> 00:00:26,956
your missed calls can trigger automations,
and your personal mobile stays private.

8
00:00:26,956 --> 00:00:28,912
Bloom already has two numbers.

9
00:00:29,762 --> 00:00:31,929
Look at the capabilities column.

10
00:00:31,929 --> 00:00:35,315
The London landline can
take calls, but in the UK,

11
00:00:35,315 --> 00:00:37,617
landline numbers can't send texts.

12
00:00:37,617 --> 00:00:39,649
The mobile number can do both.

13
00:00:39,649 --> 00:00:43,576
If you want to text customers,
you need a number with SMS.

14
00:00:43,576 --> 00:00:46,827
Texting is included on
the Growth and Pro plans.

15
00:00:47,676 --> 00:00:49,925
To add a number, click Add Number.

16
00:00:49,925 --> 00:00:52,041
Choose the country and the type.

17
00:00:52,041 --> 00:00:55,216
Local numbers look familiar
to nearby customers.

18
00:00:55,216 --> 00:00:56,803
Mobile numbers can text.

19
00:00:56,803 --> 00:00:59,382
Toll-free numbers are free for callers.

20
00:01:00,233 --> 00:01:02,729
Pick a number from the list and click Buy.

21
00:01:02,729 --> 00:01:05,462
You'll see what it
supports and what it costs.

22
00:01:05,462 --> 00:01:09,860
The monthly rental and your call and
text usage come out of your wallet at

23
00:01:09,860 --> 00:01:10,811
wholesale rates.

24
00:01:10,811 --> 00:01:13,128
Click Confirm purchase, and it's yours.

25
00:01:13,979 --> 00:01:15,970
Now let's decide where calls go.

26
00:01:15,970 --> 00:01:18,024
Click Configure on the main line.

27
00:01:18,024 --> 00:01:21,384
In Forward calls to, enter
the phone that should ring.

28
00:01:21,384 --> 00:01:22,939
Here it's Sarah's mobile.

29
00:01:23,789 --> 00:01:27,345
Pass caller's number controls
caller ID on forwarded calls.

30
00:01:27,345 --> 00:01:31,986
Switched on, your mobile shows the
customer's number, not your Kyntlo number.

31
00:01:31,986 --> 00:01:36,507
The whisper message tells you it's a
business call before you're connected,

32
00:01:36,507 --> 00:01:38,194
so you answer the right way.

33
00:01:39,045 --> 00:01:41,741
If you record calls,
switch on Record calls,

34
00:01:41,741 --> 00:01:44,436
and let callers know
they're being recorded.

35
00:01:44,436 --> 00:01:48,051
Choose how long it rings before
voicemail, then click Save.

36
00:01:48,902 --> 00:01:51,940
Below the list is your
default outbound number.

37
00:01:51,940 --> 00:01:56,012
This is the caller ID customers
see when you call or text them,

38
00:01:56,012 --> 00:01:58,727
unless a team member has their own number.

39
00:01:58,727 --> 00:02:01,183
Use the number customers already know.

40
00:02:02,034 --> 00:02:03,801
Next, the Trust Center tab.

41
00:02:03,801 --> 00:02:08,973
Carriers want to know who is behind a
number before they deliver your calls and

42
00:02:08,973 --> 00:02:09,365
texts.

43
00:02:09,365 --> 00:02:13,686
Your customer profile uses the
details from your business profile.

44
00:02:13,686 --> 00:02:18,595
UK numbers also need a regulatory
bundle, a proof of your business address.

45
00:02:18,595 --> 00:02:20,100
Both are approved here.

46
00:02:20,951 --> 00:02:26,994
If you text customers from a US local
number, you also need A2P 10DLC registration.

47
00:02:26,994 --> 00:02:32,892
You register your brand, then a campaign
describing the messages you send and how

48
00:02:32,892 --> 00:02:33,911
people opt in.

49
00:02:33,911 --> 00:02:37,843
Until it's approved, US
carriers may block your texts.

50
00:02:38,693 --> 00:02:40,795
Already have a number customers know?

51
00:02:40,795 --> 00:02:43,068
Use Number Porting to move it to Kyntlo.

52
00:02:43,068 --> 00:02:46,761
Keep it active with your old
provider until the move is complete,

53
00:02:46,761 --> 00:02:48,579
so you don't miss a single call.

54
00:02:49,430 --> 00:02:50,481
Here's a pro tip.

55
00:02:50,481 --> 00:02:54,622
Put your Kyntlo number everywhere
customers find you: your website,

56
00:02:54,622 --> 00:02:58,022
your Google profile, your
ads and your email signature.

57
00:02:58,022 --> 00:03:02,967
That way every call is tracked, and missed
calls can get an automatic text back.

58
00:03:03,819 --> 00:03:05,525
Your phone system is ready!

59
00:03:05,525 --> 00:03:10,769
Next, we'll set up your own email sending
domain, so your emails land in the inbox.

60
00:03:10,769 --> 00:03:11,654
See you there.
